    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d805">

                <pb facs="0914" n="821" xml:id="pg821"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1731/108</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 917</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-07-05">July 5, 1935</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        11.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of the
                    Department’s telegram No. 28 of July 3, 6 p.m., 1935, in regard to the trade
                    agreement to be negotiated with Nicaragua, I have the honor to inform the
                    Department that this morning I called upon the Minister for Foreign Affairs,
                    handed him personally one English and one Spanish copy of the general provisions
                    supplied with the Department’s instruction No. 232 of March 28, 1935,<anchor
                        n="16" xml:id="d805-f1"/> and reserved the right to make further
                    changes.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur Bliss Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
